      {
        "id": 161966,
        "name": "Honolulu Blue",
        "username": "Honolulu_Blue",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/ecae2f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-13T11:47:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"riff.freelance\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/riff.freelance/48/2050_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> riff.freelance:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think it says something that it's kinda hard to think of a team of 5 that would be hard pressed to be full of fail. Now a 3 man team (esecially against certain villians) would be easier to pick.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think it's hard too.&nbsp; I rarely play 5 hero teams because they generally make the game so easy.&nbsp; I'd like to hear your (and others') thoughts on 3 hero teams.&nbsp; I've been running with the available Dark Watch characters from the video game (Fixer, Expatriette, Nightmist) and though they do have their challenges and anti-synergies, they're probably not the worst around - at least against most villains.</p>",
